      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the back gesture should work on the real focus window and wait when there is no focus window. When the new back gesture feature is not enabled on the android T , CompatOnBackInvokedCallback is registered and its function is to inject a back key to app, in this case it is useful for this problem(Bug:260203909) to re-inject the back key to InputManager if no focus , However, if the app sets its own callback, then the callback may be applied to a window that is not actually the focus window, which can cause some problems.",
